# Rank 1422 / CVE-2025-48949 (navidrome, CWE-89): the native REST API's list
# endpoints accept a `_filters` JSON object in the query string. deluan/rest's GetAll
# decodes it into rest.QueryOptions.Filters and navidrome's
# persistence/sql_restful.go parseRestFilters walks the map, looking each key up in
# the repository's filterMappings table and calling the registered filterFunc with
# the client's value:
#
#	if ff, ok := r.filterMappings[f]; ok {
#		if filter := ff(f, v); filter != nil {
#			filters = append(filters, filter)
#		}
#
# NewArtistRepository registers "role" -> roleFilter, and roleFilter reads:
#
#	func roleFilter(_ string, role any) Sqlizer {
#		return NotEq{fmt.Sprintf("stats ->> '$.%v'", role): nil}
#	}
#
# squirrel's NotEq is a map whose *key is the SQL expression* and whose value is the
# bound argument -- `sq.Eq{"id": 1}` renders `id = ?` with 1 in the argument list --
# so only the value half is ever parameterised and the key is copied into the
# statement as SQL text. Here the key is built with fmt.Sprintf from the client's
# filter value, and that value lands inside a quoted JSON path in a comparison the
# builder emits unquoted, so closing the quote and the parenthesis continues the
# statement. The fixed revision's own regression test names the payload: a role of
# `artist') SELECT LIKE(CHAR(65,66,67,68,69,70,71),UPPER(HEX(RANDOMBLOB(500000000/2))))--`
# reaches SQLite as executable SQL. Any authenticated user can send it; there is no
# admin gate on GET /api/artist.
#
# The fixed revision (b19d5f0d3e079639904cac95735228f445c798b6) adds the allowlist the
# identifier slot has always needed -- there is no placeholder form for a column,
# table or JSON-path identifier in any dialect -- and fails closed:
#
#	if role, ok := role.(string); ok {
#		if _, ok := model.AllRoles[role]; ok {
#			return NotEq{fmt.Sprintf("stats ->> '$.%v'", role): nil}
#		}
#	}
#	return Eq{"1": 2}
#
# Detection is code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation (VYQL-INJ-152, CWE-89),
# which existed for Python  and is emitted for Go as well by the new
# goSqlBuilderConditionKeyInterpolation binding in
# vyql/bindings/go/sqlBuilderConditionKeyInterpolation.vyql. Nothing is minted: no
# new concept, no new rule, no new rule ID.
#
# The binding is written from squirrel's documentation, not from this repository. It
# asks three things of a Go function: a
# condition-map type is named (Eq, NotEq, Lt, LtOrEq, Gt, GtOrEq, Like, NotLike,
# ILike, NotILike -- matched as exact identifier tokens, so strings.EqualFold does not
# satisfy "Eq"); a composite-literal *key* in that function is a formatting call
# (fmt.Sprintf, fmt.Sprint, fmt.Sprintln, strings.Join, strings.Replace,
# strings.ReplaceAll) rather than a string literal; and the body contains no allowlist
# -- no indexed set-membership lookup, no slices.Contains / slices.Index /
# sort.SearchStrings, no lib/pq identifier quoter. The Go frontend records a
# composite-literal key only when it resolves to a path, which is what makes the
# "key is computed" fact available at all: `NotEq{fmt.Sprintf(...): nil}` carries
# `field:fmt.Sprintf` and `NotEq{"stats ->> '$.artist'": nil}` carries no field token.
# A key built by `+` concatenation carries none either, so that spelling is outside
# the shape's reach; it is a stated gap, not a claim that concatenation is safe.
#
# The binding also carries `dependency("github.com/Masterminds/squirrel")`, which names
# the builder the shape is written from but is measured not to narrow anything: a Go
# module path's package root is its hostname (extract/sca/identity.go PackageRoot), and
# packageGate.matches tests the hostname prefix, so a go.mod requiring only
# github.com/deluan/rest satisfies a requirement naming github.com/Masterminds/squirrel.
# A minimal module with the vulnerable function and that one unrelated requirement
# reports; the same module with no go.mod at all does not, because there is then no
# package evidence of any kind. Precision therefore rests on the match, not the gate,
# and is measured that way.
#
# Measured with `--cache off`, counts as the union of three runs. The whole navidrome
# tree at the vulnerable revision b19d5f0d3e^ reports 182 findings and the fixed revision
# b19d5f0d3e reports 181; the single difference is one VYQL-INJ-152 row at
# persistence/artist_repository.go:131, roleFilter. Removing the binding gives 181 on
# the vulnerable revision too, so the delta is the binding and nothing else.
#
# Collateral is enumerated exhaustively rather than sampled, because the shape's
# reachable set is small and greppable: a map literal whose key is a formatting call.
# Across all 985 repository clones under /tmp/cve-work, 165 Go composite literals hold
# a formatting call at all and exactly 9 hold one in the *key* position; deduplicated,
# that is three real sources plus this rank's own repros, and all three are squirrel
# condition maps.
#
# kubeflow pipelines' getPipelineVersionByCol
# (backend/src/apiserver/storage/pipeline_store.go:1109,
# `sq.Eq{fmt.Sprintf("pipeline_versions.%s", colName): colVal}`) is declined, because
# the same function indexes `versions[0]` and the allowlist negation is deliberately
# generous about an indexed lookup. mattermost-plugin-playbooks' buildTeamLimitExpr
# (server/sqlstore/playbook_run.go:1060,
# `sq.Eq{fmt.Sprintf("%s.TeamID", tableName): teamID}`) is reported, 1 row of 48
# findings on that tree -- a genuine instance of the same construct, a table
# identifier formatted into a condition key with no name check in the function, which
# is exactly what the concept's reviewCondition describes.
#
# Sixteen Go trees are scanned whole for the same rule and hold one row between them,
# the playbooks one: argo-cd (0 of 7296 findings), minder (0 of 348), mcp-toolbox
# (0 of 78), chaos-mesh (0 of 119), grpc-gateway (0 of 158),
# exposure-notifications-server (0 of 171), nats-server (0 of 148), memos (0 of 40),
# localai, melange, mailpit, oidc, jwt and the msteams, jira and playbooks
# mattermost plugins. lxd and waypoint exceed the 180s scan budget whole and are
# covered by the grep enumeration instead; neither holds an occurrence of the shape.
#
# Pool row: correct as recorded. It is a "Merge commit from fork" security merge and
# `git show` reads it in full -- two files, the one-function fix and its regression
# test. The vulnerable construct is present at b19d5f0d3e^ and the allowlist is
# present at b19d5f0d3e.

test "rank1422: a squirrel condition-map key formatted from a filter value is an unvalidated SQL identifier"
  lang go
  file persistence/artist_repository.go
  expect VYQL-INJ-152
  expect_review code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation
  code
  ```
  package persistence

  import (
  	"fmt"

  	. "github.com/Masterminds/squirrel"
  )

  func roleFilter(_ string, role any) Sqlizer {
  	return NotEq{fmt.Sprintf("stats ->> '$.%v'", role): nil}
  }
  ```
  file go.mod
  code
  ```
  module github.com/navidrome/navidrome

  go 1.24

  require (
      github.com/Masterminds/squirrel v1.5.4
      github.com/deluan/rest v0.0.0-20211102003136-6260bc399cbf
  )
  ```

test "rank1422: the same key behind a role-name allowlist is not reported"
  lang go
  file persistence/artist_repository.go
  reject VYQL-INJ-152
  reject_review code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation
  code
  ```
  package persistence

  import (
  	"fmt"

  	. "github.com/Masterminds/squirrel"
  	"github.com/navidrome/navidrome/model"
  )

  func roleFilter(_ string, role any) Sqlizer {
  	if role, ok := role.(string); ok {
  		if _, ok := model.AllRoles[role]; ok {
  			return NotEq{fmt.Sprintf("stats ->> '$.%v'", role): nil}
  		}
  	}
  	return Eq{"1": 2}
  }
  ```
  file go.mod
  code
  ```
  module github.com/navidrome/navidrome

  go 1.24

  require (
      github.com/Masterminds/squirrel v1.5.4
      github.com/deluan/rest v0.0.0-20211102003136-6260bc399cbf
  )
  ```

